                "reply_count": 3,
                "retweet_count": 7,
                "source": "Twitter for iPhone",
                "text": "Ensuring veterans can access high-quality healthcare to live healthy lives should be one of Congress\u2019s highest priorities.\n\nI\u2019ve been working across the aisle to make it a reality for Southwest Washington veterans \u2013 because they put their lives on the line to protect freedom and democracy.\n\nWhere you choose to live shouldn\u2019t impact the care you can access, so I introduced a bipartisan bill to expand transportation services for rural veterans to more easily get to their medical appointments \u2013 and I testified in support of it before the House Veterans Affairs Committee.\n\nI also directly urged the VA Secretary to listen to the calls of Lewis County veterans to reopen a clinic \u2013 and I co-led the VET MEDS Act, which is now law to support veterans\u2019 access to VA-certified specialists and examiners in rural and high-need communities.",
                "text_lang": "en",
                "text_tagged_users": null,
                "text_tagged_users_ids": null,
                "text_tags": null,
                "timestamp": 1730571860,
                "view_count": 2435
            },
